-- ============================================================================
-- FC8 ASSOCIATE DEEP SEED: Metering, Control Valves & Storage, beginner tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: THE METER RUN. One orifice result read line by line;
-- the discharge coefficient computed rather than assumed, across beta and
-- Reynolds number; the expansibility and what it is worth; sizing the plate
-- and the two refusals at the ends of its bracket; the permanent loss, the
-- turbine's gross volume and the straight-run table with its withheld column;
-- the transmitter whose accuracy is quoted on span; and the uncertainty budget
-- whose dominant term is a result with a margin.
--
-- THE ENGINE FACT THIS TIER OWNS. The orifice equation is simple and its
-- UNCERTAINTY is the subject. The dominant term of the budget changes name
-- down the span, and the engine returns whether its lead is clear.
--
-- WITHHELD, taught as a limit and never graded in any tier: the straight-run
-- requirement for two elbows in different planes. The capstone grades a beta,
-- a differential, a transmitter pair, a stated budget and a gross turbine
-- volume, none of which reads a straight-run column or a correction table this
-- package does not carry. The tier was audited question by question against
-- the digest and the engine before seeding (AUDIT-beginner.md).
-- ============================================================================

